    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d248">

                <pb facs="0376" n="277" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg277"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">632.6531/26: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-07-20T20:00:00-04:00">July 20, 1936—8 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>101. Your 167, July 17, 5 p.m. Aranha is cabling President Vargas immediately and
                    is following up his cable by an air mail letter. He is insisting in these
                    communications that the Brazilian Government refrain <pb facs="0377" n="278"
                        xml:id="pg278"/> from entering into any further treaties similar in any
                    sense to that recently entered into with Germany.</p>
                <p>I suggest that for the time being you limit yourself to the endeavor to obtain
                    from Dr. Macedo Soares accurate information as to what project, if any, the
                    Brazilian Government is contemplating entering into with Italy. Aranha believes
                    that he will receive correct information by cable from the President within the
                    next 2 days.</p>
                <p>Please continue to cable me fully all information which you may obtain.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
